(2730258, 376067, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m commenting on photos I voted low since people keep wishing they got comments on their low scoring shots.  As IR eye-candy (I assume this is IR) always seems to do well, I''m pretty sure this shot will score decently but nontheless...  <br/> <br/>The colors in this photo do not work.  Browns and blues don''t have to be lifeless, but these are.  There is gothic and nightmarish and there is boring.  Unfortunately this photo finds itself in the latter category.  Composition-wise, this shot is not from the perspective of the ground up.  It is from the side of the building straight over.  All those flying buttresses there beg to have you push your nose up against the side of that building and take a shot up the side or front.  There is also a lot of interesting detail all over the building that would have been better served by shooting from an angle that shows more of the side.  A lot of interesting stuff here sacrificed to blue trees and grass and a monolithic view of a building.  Maybe it''s what you were going for, I don''t know.  Overall not a bad shot, not to my liking, and borderline dnmc but good effort.</td>', 'I''m commenting on photos I voted low since people keep wishing they got comments on their low scoring shots.  As IR eye-candy (I assume this is IR) always seems to do well, I''m pretty sure this shot will score decently but nontheless...   The colors in this photo do not work.  Browns and blues don''t have to be lifeless, but these are.  There is gothic and nightmarish and there is boring.  Unfortunately this photo finds itself in the latter category.  Composition-wise, this shot is not from the perspective of the ground up.  It is from the side of the building straight over.  All those flying buttresses there beg to have you push your nose up against the side of that building and take a shot up the side or front.  There is also a lot of interesting detail all over the building that would have been better served by shooting from an angle that shows more of the side.  A lot of interesting stuff here sacrificed to blue trees and grass and a monolithic view of a building.  Maybe it''s what you were going for, I don''t know.  Overall not a bad shot, not to my liking, and borderline dnmc but good effort.', '2006-08-15 17:49:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730260, 376696, 62095, '<td valign="top">Oh dear.  The datestamp is massively distracting (Outside of the challenge itself, I would turn that feature off, because you''re blighting the pictures and the information is contained within the exif data so you don''t even need the stamp.) Then you''ve got an angle that includes a light switch and the top right hand corner of a picture frame or similar. The lamp itself is kinda fuzzy along the left side, and very dark.   The photo meets the challenge, but I''m still going to have to go low I''m afraid.</td>', 'Oh dear.  The datestamp is massively distracting (Outside of the challenge itself, I would turn that feature off, because you''re blighting the pictures and the information is contained within the exif data so you don''t even need the stamp.) Then you''ve got an angle that includes a light switch and the top right hand corner of a picture frame or similar. The lamp itself is kinda fuzzy along the left side, and very dark.   The photo meets the challenge, but I''m still going to have to go low I''m afraid.', '2006-08-15 17:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730262, 377236, 62095, '<td valign="top">Great movement on the grass.</td>', 'Great movement on the grass.', '2006-08-15 17:50:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730264, 375988, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m going back through and trying to comment on shots I voted low.  I don''t care for the high-key look of this shot because parts of her skin are so overexposed as to have disappeared completely.  More to the point, there''s nothing about this photo that is shot from the perspective of the ground up.  It''s a straight on shot focused at, of all places, her knee.  With such gothic looking boots covered with such great detail, perhaps a more interesting photo would have been up the front or side of the boot.  Who can say.  Good effort.</td>', 'I''m going back through and trying to comment on shots I voted low.  I don''t care for the high-key look of this shot because parts of her skin are so overexposed as to have disappeared completely.  More to the point, there''s nothing about this photo that is shot from the perspective of the ground up.  It''s a straight on shot focused at, of all places, her knee.  With such gothic looking boots covered with such great detail, perhaps a more interesting photo would have been up the front or side of the boot.  Who can say.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 17:51:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730272, 375595, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m going back through and commenting on shots I voted low.  Pretty colors in this shot is all it hs going for it.  This doesn''t really show the perspective of from the ground up as it''s pretty much a straight shot at the horizon with a lense that happened to catch a bunch of sky in the process.  Composition-wise there is nothing here to look at other than the blue gradient.  It just doesn''t trip my trigger but, most importantly, is a long stretch for being relevant to the challenge.  Good effort.</td>', 'I''m going back through and commenting on shots I voted low.  Pretty colors in this shot is all it hs going for it.  This doesn''t really show the perspective of from the ground up as it''s pretty much a straight shot at the horizon with a lense that happened to catch a bunch of sky in the process.  Composition-wise there is nothing here to look at other than the blue gradient.  It just doesn''t trip my trigger but, most importantly, is a long stretch for being relevant to the challenge.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 17:53:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730273, 374509, 61818, '<td valign="top">This photo has some issues.  The composition is not interesting.  Some of the clouds on the right side are blown out.  Backlighting the pole doesn''t really work well here because it just ends up looking like a jumbled mess on top of a big black mark in the photo.  I''m commenting on photos I voted low on as people cry for insight into why they got a low vote.  So not being harsh, but there it is.</td>', 'This photo has some issues.  The composition is not interesting.  Some of the clouds on the right side are blown out.  Backlighting the pole doesn''t really work well here because it just ends up looking like a jumbled mess on top of a big black mark in the photo.  I''m commenting on photos I voted low on as people cry for insight into why they got a low vote.  So not being harsh, but there it is.', '2006-08-15 17:53:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730342, 375730, 61818, '<td valign="top">I am going through and leaving comments on photos I voted low.  Biggest problem here is that it doesn''t meet the challenge of shooting something from the perspective of the ground up.  This is a shot pretty much on the level with your subject.  So there''s a big mark against though I suppose hairs can be split and degrees of ascent argued.  Setting that aside, the foreground lighting detracts from the lights in the one house which would otherwise draw my attention quickly and make me think about that part of the photo.  What''s happening in there, that house looks alive, etc - things that let me take this photo and draw my own conlusions about it.  Also looks like the photo is a bit out of focus or suffers from a little motion blur, hard to say, but nothing on that house is looking to crisp.  A lot of that combines together to make the only focal point here the two pieces of overexposed light by the door and in the window - not very interesting.<br/> <br/>Good effort.</td>', 'I am going through and leaving comments on photos I voted low.  Biggest problem here is that it doesn''t meet the challenge of shooting something from the perspective of the ground up.  This is a shot pretty much on the level with your subject.  So there''s a big mark against though I suppose hairs can be split and degrees of ascent argued.  Setting that aside, the foreground lighting detracts from the lights in the one house which would otherwise draw my attention quickly and make me think about that part of the photo.  What''s happening in there, that house looks alive, etc - things that let me take this photo and draw my own conlusions about it.  Also looks like the photo is a bit out of focus or suffers from a little motion blur, hard to say, but nothing on that house is looking to crisp.  A lot of that combines together to make the only focal point here the two pieces of overexposed light by the door and in the window - not very interesting. Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:09:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730345, 377540, 50674, '<td valign="top">I wish this shot was bigger, it is really difficult to judge a shot this small, try to go for 640 next time :)</td>', 'I wish this shot was bigger, it is really difficult to judge a shot this small, try to go for 640 next time :)', '2006-08-15 18:10:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730354, 376995, 50674, '<td valign="top">The black background is not the best background for this beautiful blue in my opinion, it takes over</td>', 'The black background is not the best background for this beautiful blue in my opinion, it takes over', '2006-08-15 18:12:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730357, 376987, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m going through and leaving comments on photos I voted low on.  This photo has some problems.  First of all it appears to be over-sharpened which gives it a very harsh, artifical look.  Composition wise there isn''t really anything here that acts as the focal point of the shot.  Cloud details are either neat-images beyond recognition or missing for some other reason, trees are backlit, the sun is barely visible, etc.  Pretty colors are always nice but they can not make a photo interesting on their own.   Here you''ve got blue and orange with very little transition between them, and the right side of the photo gets pretty heavy on the darkness with the trees and that big cloud.  Good effort.</td>', 'I''m going through and leaving comments on photos I voted low on.  This photo has some problems.  First of all it appears to be over-sharpened which gives it a very harsh, artifical look.  Composition wise there isn''t really anything here that acts as the focal point of the shot.  Cloud details are either neat-images beyond recognition or missing for some other reason, trees are backlit, the sun is barely visible, etc.  Pretty colors are always nice but they can not make a photo interesting on their own.   Here you''ve got blue and orange with very little transition between them, and the right side of the photo gets pretty heavy on the darkness with the trees and that big cloud.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:13:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730368, 376668, 61818, '<td valign="top">Part of the challenge of showing somethign from the persective of the ground up is actually showing that the persepctive is from the ground up.  I give benefit of the doubt that you were standing underneath this bug and shot upwards but the angles of the web strands, the fact that there is a fly on the right hanging ''down'' - all these things really give the impression that this was pretty much shot straight on horizontally.  Little more DOF would be nice to make out more of the web.  Hard to make out anything on the spider itself other than the yellow blob on the back.  Overall nothing to really interest the viewer here or move the eye around the shot.  Biggest drawback though is the perspective thing.  Good effort.</td>', 'Part of the challenge of showing somethign from the persective of the ground up is actually showing that the persepctive is from the ground up.  I give benefit of the doubt that you were standing underneath this bug and shot upwards but the angles of the web strands, the fact that there is a fly on the right hanging ''down'' - all these things really give the impression that this was pretty much shot straight on horizontally.  Little more DOF would be nice to make out more of the web.  Hard to make out anything on the spider itself other than the yellow blob on the back.  Overall nothing to really interest the viewer here or move the eye around the shot.  Biggest drawback though is the perspective thing.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:16:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730369, 377556, 50674, '<td valign="top">I am not sure that I would have chosen b&amp;w and there is nothing much happening even if there is a huge vehicle here. I like the angle you chose.</td>', 'I am not sure that I would have chosen b&w and there is nothing much happening even if there is a huge vehicle here. I like the angle you chose.', '2006-08-15 18:16:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730373, 374865, 50674, '<td valign="top">i really like this one, but how it fits the challenge is hard to figure :) (for me at least)</td>', 'i really like this one, but how it fits the challenge is hard to figure :) (for me at least)', '2006-08-15 18:17:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730381, 376617, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m leaving comments on shots I voted low, so here we go.  Biggest problem here is not meeting the challenge in the least.  This photo isn''t shot from the perspective of the ground up, it''s show from above looking down.  That is a huge problem.  Don''t care for how the kid''s upper body is cropped off.  I think there might be some promise in a shot like this if shot from below, from a different angle that includes what is probably a really interesting expression on the kid''s face, doesn''t overwhelm the eye with the boring gray of the skatepark concrete, etc.  Good effort.</td>', 'I''m leaving comments on shots I voted low, so here we go.  Biggest problem here is not meeting the challenge in the least.  This photo isn''t shot from the perspective of the ground up, it''s show from above looking down.  That is a huge problem.  Don''t care for how the kid''s upper body is cropped off.  I think there might be some promise in a shot like this if shot from below, from a different angle that includes what is probably a really interesting expression on the kid''s face, doesn''t overwhelm the eye with the boring gray of the skatepark concrete, etc.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:18:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730391, 375028, 61818, '<td valign="top">Bigest problem here is not shooting ''from the perspective of the ground up''.  Mountains and some sky in the background don''t outweight the fact that this appears to have been shot from eye level and more or less looking straight forward.  Lots of interesting detail here that might have really made this image pop.  Kneel in that creek, shoot up from the water and get those wildflowers in the foreground with the peeaks jutting up behind them.  The long sloping meadow is nice, all of nature is, but nature can be mundane too and to me this falls in that category.  A lot of nice stuff, nothing in particular to focus on, etc.  Good effort.</td>', 'Bigest problem here is not shooting ''from the perspective of the ground up''.  Mountains and some sky in the background don''t outweight the fact that this appears to have been shot from eye level and more or less looking straight forward.  Lots of interesting detail here that might have really made this image pop.  Kneel in that creek, shoot up from the water and get those wildflowers in the foreground with the peeaks jutting up behind them.  The long sloping meadow is nice, all of nature is, but nature can be mundane too and to me this falls in that category.  A lot of nice stuff, nothing in particular to focus on, etc.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:21:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730395, 375369, 61818, '<td valign="top">This is a nice photo, and I like the BW processing.  It''s also clearly shot dead on level with the guy so there goes ''from the perspective of the ground up''.  Kneeling down behind him and shooting up with those mountains in the background would have made this an excellent photo for the challenge.  On a relatively minor note, a litle more contrast to bring out the details on those peaks would be welome here as well.  Good effort.</td>', 'This is a nice photo, and I like the BW processing.  It''s also clearly shot dead on level with the guy so there goes ''from the perspective of the ground up''.  Kneeling down behind him and shooting up with those mountains in the background would have made this an excellent photo for the challenge.  On a relatively minor note, a litle more contrast to bring out the details on those peaks would be welome here as well.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:22:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730406, 377486, 61818, '<td valign="top">Going through and trying to comment on shots I voted low on.  I voted this shot low because, while certainly meeting the challenge, it is a very, very boring photo.  The lack of colors here is tough on the eye.  Little sprinkling of green among the leaves crushed between a dead sky and the neutral tones of the tree itself.  There also look to be some interesting shapes up in the tree so I''m thinking moving back a bit from the trunk would have kept your persective for the challenge while adding some things for the eye to move around on in the photo.  The trunk itself overwhelms this picture while at the same tim eoffering almost no detail to study/get interested in.  There are probably some nice textures on there that could have been brought out by crisper focus and some increased contrast. Good effort.</td>', 'Going through and trying to comment on shots I voted low on.  I voted this shot low because, while certainly meeting the challenge, it is a very, very boring photo.  The lack of colors here is tough on the eye.  Little sprinkling of green among the leaves crushed between a dead sky and the neutral tones of the tree itself.  There also look to be some interesting shapes up in the tree so I''m thinking moving back a bit from the trunk would have kept your persective for the challenge while adding some things for the eye to move around on in the photo.  The trunk itself overwhelms this picture while at the same tim eoffering almost no detail to study/get interested in.  There are probably some nice textures on there that could have been brought out by crisper focus and some increased contrast. Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:25:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730418, 377421, 61818, '<td valign="top">Perspective is pretty much the exact opposite of the challenge.  Crop is too tight, nothing here to move the eye around the image.  Maybe getting down on your knees, shooting from an angle that does look as if you are looking up at this thing, including all of it in the frame or moving it off to a side, something.</td>', 'Perspective is pretty much the exact opposite of the challenge.  Crop is too tight, nothing here to move the eye around the image.  Maybe getting down on your knees, shooting from an angle that does look as if you are looking up at this thing, including all of it in the frame or moving it off to a side, something.', '2006-08-15 18:27:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730425, 376041, 61818, '<td valign="top">The persective here is not from the ground up, so that immediately hurts the score.  Colors could be a bit more vibrant and the flower itself could be sharper in focus.  Some interesting detail on that thing.</td>', 'The persective here is not from the ground up, so that immediately hurts the score.  Colors could be a bit more vibrant and the flower itself could be sharper in focus.  Some interesting detail on that thing.', '2006-08-15 18:28:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730432, 376805, 61818, '<td valign="top">Images the size of a postage stamp dont'' score well with me, and this one has the added disadvantage of not even attempting to meet the ''from the ground up'' persective as challenged (unless bees have taken to flying on their sides).  All of which is a shame because I think this is probably a beautiful photo.  The colors work extremely well, it appears to be in perfect focus, the composition is excellent, and you captured the bee at the perfect moment.  Really I would like to kick you for making me vote low on such a nice photo.  Good effort.</td>', 'Images the size of a postage stamp dont'' score well with me, and this one has the added disadvantage of not even attempting to meet the ''from the ground up'' persective as challenged (unless bees have taken to flying on their sides).  All of which is a shame because I think this is probably a beautiful photo.  The colors work extremely well, it appears to be in perfect focus, the composition is excellent, and you captured the bee at the perfect moment.  Really I would like to kick you for making me vote low on such a nice photo.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:30:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730446, 377407, 61818, '<td valign="top">Perspective here isn''t from the ground up, it''s from the ground straight forward.  Flash so harsh in the foreground detracts greatly from what otherwise would have been a very moody shot with the sunset under that dark cloud and the lightning bolt.  I like how the rails head off into infinity.  Between the flash and, most importantly, the angle this was shot at I''m afraid this didn''t score well with me.  Good effort.</td>', 'Perspective here isn''t from the ground up, it''s from the ground straight forward.  Flash so harsh in the foreground detracts greatly from what otherwise would have been a very moody shot with the sunset under that dark cloud and the lightning bolt.  I like how the rails head off into infinity.  Between the flash and, most importantly, the angle this was shot at I''m afraid this didn''t score well with me.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:37:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730449, 374641, 61818, '<td valign="top">Sort of from the ground up.  Most interesting part of the flower is out of focus.  Sky is blown out or darn close.  Nothing really interests my eyes here.  Good effort.</td>', 'Sort of from the ground up.  Most interesting part of the flower is out of focus.  Sky is blown out or darn close.  Nothing really interests my eyes here.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:38:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730452, 377096, 61818, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if ''looking up'' necessarily meets the challenge of shooting something from the perspective of the ground up.  Setting that aside, the only thing to look at in the photo is the bird and the bird is out of focus.  MAybe you were going for a soft look.  I submit soft focus shots purposely and routinely get reamed for doing so, so I''m not holding it against you persay.  However when there is simply nothing else in the shot and you can''t make out any detail on the one thing that is in the shot you don''t really end up with an interesting photograph.  Good effort.</td>', 'I don''t know if ''looking up'' necessarily meets the challenge of shooting something from the perspective of the ground up.  Setting that aside, the only thing to look at in the photo is the bird and the bird is out of focus.  MAybe you were going for a soft look.  I submit soft focus shots purposely and routinely get reamed for doing so, so I''m not holding it against you persay.  However when there is simply nothing else in the shot and you can''t make out any detail on the one thing that is in the shot you don''t really end up with an interesting photograph.  Good effort.', '2006-08-15 18:40:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2730593, 377447, 55330, '<td valign="top">Im a sucker for IR shots</td>', 'Im a sucker for IR shots', '2006-08-15 19:13:17.000000', NULL, 1),
