(2733751, 375997, 24454, '<td valign="top">I AM so happy THIS WON a ribbon.  It was definitely one of my top 3 favorites in this challenge!  I''d say, what separates you from those that are technically perfect -- the real pros -- is that YOU have an award winning, 2nd-place ribbon and they don''t :)   CONGRATULATIONS!  This is just awesome!</td>', 'I AM so happy THIS WON a ribbon.  It was definitely one of my top 3 favorites in this challenge!  I''d say, what separates you from those that are technically perfect -- the real pros -- is that YOU have an award winning, 2nd-place ribbon and they don''t :)   CONGRATULATIONS!  This is just awesome!', '2006-08-16 12:53:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2733765, 377105, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  I was hoping you''d get higher :(  I think it should have been front page.</td>', 'Congratulations!  I was hoping you''d get higher :(  I think it should have been front page.', '2006-08-16 12:57:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2733770, 377225, 27137, '<td valign="top">Well done Marc<br/></td>', 'Well done Marc', '2006-08-16 12:59:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2733779, 376712, 24454, '<td valign="top">Well.. .I have to chime in and say that I totally disagree with Imagineeer and Kemptonreporter.  I think this photo is exactly why good photographers need to not be so anal and rigid about any "rule" (and the rule of thirds one is so incredibly over-emphasized here). . .and realize that a great photo <i>can</i> take all sorts of compositions.  It''s the eye of the great ones that "sees it" and throws the "rules" out the window.    This photo is incredible, and the perspective of that upward winding cobblestone road against that dramatic sky with these beautiful blue tones.   I think if ever there was a deserving blue ribbon this is it!   And way to go, waiting till you got "the one", entering it and winning blue on your first call!  You rock, and this is totally awesome!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-16 12:04:28.</i></td>', 'Well.. .I have to chime in and say that I totally disagree with Imagineeer and Kemptonreporter.  I think this photo is exactly why good photographers need to not be so anal and rigid about any "rule" (and the rule of thirds one is so incredibly over-emphasized here). . .and realize that a great photo can take all sorts of compositions.  It''s the eye of the great ones that "sees it" and throws the "rules" out the window.    This photo is incredible, and the perspective of that upward winding cobblestone road against that dramatic sky with these beautiful blue tones.   I think if ever there was a deserving blue ribbon this is it!   And way to go, waiting till you got "the one", entering it and winning blue on your first call!  You rock, and this is totally awesome!', '2006-08-16 13:02:36.000000', '2006-08-16 13:04:28.000000', 0),
(2733794, 374405, 48717, '<td valign="top">Look at you - I think you are hooked!  Very creative.</td>', 'Look at you - I think you are hooked!  Very creative.', '2006-08-16 13:06:52.000000', NULL, 0),
