(2750772, 376039, 46336, '<td valign="top">Hi Enzo, <br/> <br/>I drew this for Critique Club but the site closed it down when they did the results refresh. I figure I owe you the Critique (anyway I had started thinking about it) so I''ve come back. <br/> <br/>Congraulations on the great score - it''s always nice to bring in what you set out for. This shot provides a magnificent sense of perspective - you have managed to get your angles just right to convey the sheer towering magnificence.Good going. The crispness and colours you have managed to achieve on the building are superb - good editing. <br/> <br/>Personally I am not a fan of the extreme blue of the sky. I would have marked you down a bit for it. Clearly many other have a different take and love it. I''m guessing the change of hue to blue won you more votes than it lose you. Still I would have preferred a more natural colour. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Paul</td>', 'Hi Enzo,  I drew this for Critique Club but the site closed it down when they did the results refresh. I figure I owe you the Critique (anyway I had started thinking about it) so I''ve come back.  Congraulations on the great score - it''s always nice to bring in what you set out for. This shot provides a magnificent sense of perspective - you have managed to get your angles just right to convey the sheer towering magnificence.Good going. The crispness and colours you have managed to achieve on the building are superb - good editing.  Personally I am not a fan of the extreme blue of the sky. I would have marked you down a bit for it. Clearly many other have a different take and love it. I''m guessing the change of hue to blue won you more votes than it lose you. Still I would have preferred a more natural colour.  CheersPaul', '2006-08-23 01:49:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2752361, 374758, 34659, '<td valign="top">What a great shot!!!  The perspective is awesome and I''m really digging the cross hair light action!  ;-)  Well done.</td>', 'What a great shot!!!  The perspective is awesome and I''m really digging the cross hair light action!  ;-)  Well done.', '2006-08-23 12:00:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2752689, 374758, 48245, '<td valign="top">This is a nice picture. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I saw it and wondered if this was our tower. What did you use to get the star effect? A filter?</td>', 'This is a nice picture. I didn''t vote in this challenge but I saw it and wondered if this was our tower. What did you use to get the star effect? A filter?', '2006-08-23 13:38:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2753994, 377427, 43340, '<td valign="top">Great use of the fisheye on one of my favorite streets in one of my favorite cities.</td>', 'Great use of the fisheye on one of my favorite streets in one of my favorite cities.', '2006-08-23 18:58:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2754830, 376419, 34938, '<td valign="top">awesome and underrated to the max...this was a great shot for the challenge</td>', 'awesome and underrated to the max...this was a great shot for the challenge', '2006-08-23 22:46:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2756313, 374421, 43191, '<td valign="top">What a cool shot shot. You''ve got a couple of great models.</td>', 'What a cool shot shot. You''ve got a couple of great models.', '2006-08-24 10:04:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2756639, 376710, 30982, '<td valign="top">What an odd looking little critter!  I like the way you chose to shoot this to sort of frame him with the branches and leaves.  Good color throughout.  As for the challenge, it may have done better had you shot from a lower angle - doesn''t look as much "up" as some might have been expecting, I''m guessing.  And VERY good work without a flash in low light!  He does look like he could use a good shampoo, though... :-)</td>', 'What an odd looking little critter!  I like the way you chose to shoot this to sort of frame him with the branches and leaves.  Good color throughout.  As for the challenge, it may have done better had you shot from a lower angle - doesn''t look as much "up" as some might have been expecting, I''m guessing.  And VERY good work without a flash in low light!  He does look like he could use a good shampoo, though... :-)', '2006-08-24 12:17:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2756735, 374773, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like it!  I always like lines/patterns kinda shots, and what I like about this one (besides the really nice clear blue sky) is the addition of the bird amidst all the lines.  In reading through the other comments, it''s intersting that some liked the bird there, some didn''t.  Good to have you back shooting - now just avoid the tranny crack ho''s, ''k?</td>', 'I like it!  I always like lines/patterns kinda shots, and what I like about this one (besides the really nice clear blue sky) is the addition of the bird amidst all the lines.  In reading through the other comments, it''s intersting that some liked the bird there, some didn''t.  Good to have you back shooting - now just avoid the tranny crack ho''s, ''k?', '2006-08-24 13:03:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2758808, 377570, 43191, '<td valign="top">LOL, this is way cute! I love shots of dogs from weird angles.</td>', 'LOL, this is way cute! I love shots of dogs from weird angles.', '2006-08-25 03:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2758949, 377201, 41337, '<td valign="top">This is pretty cool.</td>', 'This is pretty cool.', '2006-08-25 04:24:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2759799, 377293, 50695, '<td valign="top">cool picture. It looks like you''re being pummeled with light... about to transform into something. It also looks like your two halves are different, one a little dark, one superbright.</td>', 'cool picture. It looks like you''re being pummeled with light... about to transform into something. It also looks like your two halves are different, one a little dark, one superbright.', '2006-08-25 14:10:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2759827, 374421, 51538, '<td valign="top">This photo was indeed one of the better (and more creative) ones of the challenge.  Keep up the good work.</td>', 'This photo was indeed one of the better (and more creative) ones of the challenge.  Keep up the good work.', '2006-08-25 14:21:52.000000', NULL, 0),
